  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: 'On the Wrist: Wearables'
  meta: "Recovered from a human wrist  \xB7  Apple Watch released April 2015"
  body: Smartwatches moved the computer from the pocket onto the skin. Their optical
    sensors read a human's pulse, motion sensors counted steps and detected falls,
    and some could record a simple electrocardiogram. The device no longer only served
    its owner; it constantly measured them.
  themeLink: Here the line between tool and body began to blur. Measuring a body
    was also the first step to keeping one alive away from their planet.
  credit: 'Model: "Watch" by Poly by Google, CC BY 3.0, via Poly Pizza. A generic
    watch, not a specific product.'
