  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: International Space Station
  meta: "Recovered in orbit  \xB7  First module launched November 1998  \xB7  Crewed
    continuously from November 2000"
  body: The International Space Station was a laboratory the size of a football field,
    orbiting about 400 km above Earth, built together by the USA, Russia, Europe,
    Japan and Canada. Humans lived on board without a break for many years, testing
    how bodies, plants and machines coped with months of weightlessness.
  themeLink: 'The station was their rehearsal room: the first place where living
    off the planet became a daily routine rather than a short trip.'
  credit: 'Model: "International Space Station" by Poly by Google, CC BY 3.0, via
    Poly Pizza. Simplified, not to scale.'
