  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: Landing on Mars
  meta: "Stylised reconstruction  \xB7  First successful Mars landing: Viking 1,
    20 July 1976"
  body: 'Landing on Mars was famously hard: the air was too thin to slow a spacecraft
    easily, but thick enough to burn it. Human landers combined heat shields, parachutes
    and rockets in a few minutes they called the "seven minutes of terror". Every
    settlement they dreamed of depended on getting this right.'
  themeLink: Before any human could live on Mars, their machines had to arrive safely
    and prepare the way. This is the doorway to the final room.
  credit: 'Model: "Lander B" by Kay Lousberg, CC0, via Poly Pizza. Stylised, not
    a model of a real mission.'
  image: {fileID: 0}
  interactPoint: {fileID: 0}
