--- !u!114 &2053263037
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2053263035}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a8c78a3dc61624f33b78b8b42697355c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MuseumExhibit
  title: iPhone (1st generation)
  meta: "Recovered in great numbers  \xB7  Apple Inc.  \xB7  Released 29 June 2007
    (US)"
  body: 'We found more of these than any other human object. The first iPhone combined
    a phone, a music player and an internet device in one slab of glass. Instead
    of a keypad it used a 3.5-inch multi-touch screen, so its controls were software
    that could change after it was bought.


    When the App Store opened in July
    2008, the device began absorbing other objects: the camera, the paper map, the
    music player, the flashlight and eventually the wallet. Most humans carried one
    everywhere; directions, payment, photos and conversation all passed through it.'
  themeLink: Our route follows human technology as it left the desk, moved into the
    pocket, onto the body, and finally off their planet. The small chips, batteries
    and sensors made for phones later flew in space (stage 3).
  credit: 'Model: "Smartphone" by smallbigsquare, CC0, via Poly Pizza. Generic smartphone
    shown at 5x scale, not an official Apple model.'
  image: {fileID: 0}
  interactPoint: {fileID: 0}
  interactRange: 3
  model: {fileID: 1522014536}
  idleSpin: 10
  sway: 1
  swayAngle: 28
  screen: {fileID: 1767828466}
  focusHighlight: {fileID: 384967124}
  keepModeOnOpen: 0
  onModeChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  musicSource: {fileID: 0}
  modes:
  - label: "2007 \xB7 Glass replaces keys"
    caption: A single touchscreen replaced the keypad. Buttons became pictures that
      software could redraw at any time.
    screenColor: {r: 0.25490198, g: 0.9137255, b: 0.92156863, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 0}
    lift: 0
    spinSpeed: 14
    music: {fileID: 0}
  - label: "2008 \xB7 Apps absorb objects"
    caption: With the App Store, one device swallowed the camera, map, music player
      and wallet now floating around it.
    screenColor: {r: 0.67058825, g: 0.4509804, b: 1, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 61564907}
    lift: 0
    spinSpeed: 30
    music: {fileID: 0}
  - label: "2013 \xB7 A phone in orbit"
    caption: NASA's PhoneSat missions (2013) flew off-the-shelf smartphones as the
      computers of tiny satellites. Pocket tech became space hardware.
    screenColor: {r: 1, g: 0.49803922, b: 0.78431374, a: 1}
    showObject: {fileID: 483287817}
    lift: 0.35
    spinSpeed: 45
    music: {fileID: 0}
